    {
      "evidence": "template/scripts/select_checks.py, `precheck_outcome` returns \"unavailable\" for a non-zero exit without `failed_groups`. `execute` prints \"continuing with the full set\". specs/platform-lifecycle/spec.md says \"SHALL stop before the full set when the precheck fails\". design.md decision 3 does not mention the tooling-error case.",
      "id": "precheck-unavailable-continues-to-full",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The spec says the lifecycle SHALL stop before the full set when the precheck fails. The implementation stops only on the `failure` outcome, meaning failed test groups were reported. A non-zero runner exit with no aggregate, or with a malformed aggregate, is classified `unavailable` and the full set continues. This is a deliberate choice recorded in a code comment and a test, but neither the spec nor design.md states it."
    }
  ],
